{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline","id":1523041,"title":"Is it plausible that an older Ancilla could have 5 dots in one Discipline?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-23T12:14:13-07:00","id":1523041,"title":"Is it plausible that an older Ancilla could have 5 dots in one Discipline?","content":"Just something I've been wondering on how likely that an older Ancilla that is slightly over two hundred years old would have mastered a single Discipline &amp; would be well versed in at least three others and what is your house rules in your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-23-2023, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T14:54:43-07:00","id":1523049,"title":"","content":"Well, unless said ancillary lived the most pampered unlife possible under the constant protection of their sire, I would consider it impossible that they DIDN'T master at least their clan discipline in more than a century.<br /> <br /> So in the case you bring, we have a two century ancilla, so borderline elder. For me, the probability that they mastered at least one discipline if not more is 99,999%","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T17:55:50-07:00","id":1523059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523049#post1523049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, unless said ancillary lived the most pampered unlife possible under the constant protection of their sire, I would consider it impossible that they DIDN'T master at least their clan discipline in more than a century.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it depends on how one defines mastery - 8-10 dice in a level 3 power can be more valuable and unlife-saving in many occasions than 5-6 in the level 5 of a discipline and not every kindred goes through the &quot;burn bright, burn faster&quot; style on existence of PC neonates (in fact some of those who manage to become elders do so by <i>actively avoiding that like the plague</i>), but yeah, with age comes experience and a measure of power, so someone a number of decades past their first century is most probably <b>not</b> worried of getting the third dot in any one favored discipline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523049#post1523049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the case you bring, we have a two century ancilla, so borderline elder. For me, the probability that they mastered at least one discipline if not more is 99,999%</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, what counts as a elder can vary depending on what city one exists and how deeply woven in the higher-scale sect matters and games of the Jyhad its kindred are. Back in 1st and 2nd ed you could see some snide commentary on how in the Americas kindred 100-200 years old would stand as elders and princes of their domains, while counting as little more than mere ancillae amidst the european halls of power where the Camarilla took form.<br /> <br /> What, though Revised would take it somewhat more at face value (possibly due to age creep from DA and signature characters), was mostly posturing and horsecrap - while not the norm, Chicago and Milwaukee had primogen that could make Valerius, Lady Anne or Gustav Brendenstein feel unconfortable and Europe as a whole went through so many wars and crises between French Revolution and the two world wars that many of their capitals and major cities might be closer to the reality of that joke than most urban centers in the New World.<br /> <br /> <br /> ANYWAY, what i meant to say is that the definition of ancilla and elder have varied between the books and that kind of reflects an IC situation in that age can reflect status, but how old is old between undead can depend on a combination of jyhad attrition and how big is the league one plays into, among other factors. 200+ years of active unlife definitely falls into the &quot;respectable into most circles&quot; level and having one or two disciplines at 4-5 would be far from strange.<br /> <br /> In fact, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cock_Robin\" target=\"_blank\">Cock Robin</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anastasz_di_Zagreb\" target=\"_blank\">Anastasz di Zagreb</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Maris_Streck\" target=\"_blank\">Maris Streck</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jan_Pieterzoon\" target=\"_blank\">Jan Pieterzoon</a> are some solid canon examples of how far can someone in this age tier stand if they have the right lineage, connections &amp;/or supporters. As an aside, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Carlak\" target=\"_blank\">Carlak</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hesha_Ruhadze\" target=\"_blank\">Hesha</a> too. I was tempted to add <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Theo_Bell\" target=\"_blank\">Theo</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aisling_Sturbridge\" target=\"_blank\">Aisling </a>too, but they are more in the 100-150 years age range.\u200b<br /> <br /> Either way, there go my thoughts and a few canon examples, hope they help or you have some fun with them.<br /> <br /> edit: also, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vidal_Jarbeaux\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a>. And while being an archon might not seem as fancy as sitting on the Justicar's chair, being someone handpicked by Inner Circle members to <i>keep tabs on a Justicar's loyalties</i>....well, that's a high-powered game all its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-09-2023, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T18:12:40-07:00","id":1523060,"title":"","content":"It all depends on how you envision the vampires of your setting. I see many PCs go for having all five dots of a particular Discipline in most games, and in these cases the PCs are still neonates. So I don't see why there wouldn't be NPC equivalents for both neonates and ancillae.<br /> <br /> I don't consider the PCs to be typical of vampire characters in terms of how quickly they advance in power, but neither do I consider them to be unheard of prodigies. When designing the NPCs of the setting, I typically divide them into several categories. About 75% will advance slower than the PCs. This makes sure that the PCs have plenty of time to shine, and they can even catch up to some older vampires in power over the course of a chronicle. About 20% of NPCs advance at roughly the same pace. These are the characters that will either be rivals or important allies of the PCs in their own age group, and to explain some of the more powerful vampires older than them. About 5% of the NPCs will advance quicker than the PCs, making them powerful and well known NPCs in the setting for older vampires, and making them dangerous rivals for the PCs if the same age group. These numbers are not based on anything other than I, as the ST, think they are a helpful tool in creating an interesting setting for the players of various challenge levels.<br /> <br /> While I don't think the By Night books do a good job at designing NPCs (they tend to have strange builds and wildly out of place powers based on their age and description), I do think it can be interesting to compare what they did. Here is a breakdown of the original Chicago By Night with neonates and ancillae having at least one Discipline at 5 dots.<br /> <br /> Neonates:<br /> Hank Cave/Saint (Presence 5), Ramrod (Protean 5), Weltmann (Presence 6), Tammy (Potence 5), Sharon (Presence 5), DuSable (Auspex 5), Erictho (Auspex 5), Hinds (Presence 5), Capone (Presence 5), Brennon (Dominate 5)<br /> <br /> Ancillae:<br /> Balthazar/Sheriff (Dominate 5), Doyle (Animalism 6), O'Leary (Auspex 5), Elzbieta (Obfuscate 5), Lodin (Dominate 6), Ballard (Dominate 5), Yaryan (Animalism 5 &amp; Obfuscate 6)<br /> <br /> So as you can see, the designers of the game did not think it odd that neonates and ancillae have 5 dots of any one Discipline, although we only have one example of an old ancillae having more than one Discipline at 5 ranks. But a lot of them have additional Disciplines at 4.<br /> <br /> I would personally reduuce some of the powers for some of these characters. Why would fairly unimportant characters that function more as background elements like Hank Cave, Sharon Payne, or Brennon Thornhill have such high Disciplines? Brennon was only supposed to have existed as a vampire for six years when CbN 13 was first published! But I don't object to interesting neonates that are supposed to be heavy hitters like Capone and DuSable have them.<br /> <br /> But I do think even neonates can have Disciplines at this level. At character creation, a person can spend enough Freebies to get one of their Disciplines to level 4, and then spend the XP to buy it up to 5 fairly early in a chronicle. Such ultra-specialization does have its drawbacks, but obviously it has a lot of attraction for some players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T19:12:26-07:00","id":1523061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523060#post1523060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't think the By Night books do a good job at designing NPCs (they tend to have strange builds and wildly out of place powers based on their age and description), I do think it can be interesting to compare what they did. Here is a breakdown of the original Chicago By Night with neonates and ancillae having at least one Discipline at 5 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too true indeed. Nowadays when i want to have something of a benchmark to compare and <i>sort of</i> balance everyone out, i use the rough guidelines from Children of Night as a starting point and then tweak here with 1-5 dots to represent the &quot;rising star&quot; power of some younger kindred punching above their weight class - and on the other side of the scale you can always use Torpor as an explanation for older kindred <b>NOT</b> to to be as ludricously powerful as their supposed age might indicate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523060#post1523060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elzbieta (Obfuscate 5),</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Random comical aside, in a friend's Chicago chronicle Elzbieta came out of torpor a little after <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cedrick_Calhoun\" target=\"_blank\">Cedrick</a> started assuming her sire's place - and proceeded to give him one of the harshest beatdowns he ever suffered in his unlife for his troubles. Only reasons the whole farse didn't come apart like a castle of cards was the fight happened out of sight underground and that Calhoun proceeded to both confess and explain himself, what helped her to calm down (not to mention probably saved him from ending in torpor or ashes). Ever since she has become Cedrick's counselor, right hand woman and &quot;acting coach&quot;, immensely helping him with settling into the role of impersonating Khalid among kindred who were acquainted with the elder for far longer than he.<br /> <br /> (It's possible that her &quot;coaching&quot; of Cedrick might have some level of grooming or transference of her past unrequited feelings toward Khalid to his understudy mixed, but that's a whole other story for him to tiptoe against....)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523060#post1523060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would personally reduce some of the powers for some of these characters. Why would fairly unimportant characters that function more as background elements like Hank Cave, Sharon Payne, or Brennon Thornhill have such high Disciplines? Brennon was only supposed to have existed as a vampire for six years when CbN was first published!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh damn, the egreriousness of Dominate 5 (Presence 5 too, but it ain't as broken imho) - seriously, the city would implode in flames just one night if a ST ever plotted something to make use of all the kindred with Conditioning &amp;/or Possession! I still remember back in the 90's spending a whole night just discussing the NPCs, whose Dominate 5 to cut down to 3 - or outright replace for two other disciplines at 2-3 (hello Sheriff) - and a bunch of other stat tweaks all around, before the first time i ever played CbN.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523060#post1523060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I do think even neonates can have Disciplines at this level. At character creation, a person can spend enough Freebies to get one of their Disciplines to level 4, and then spend the XP to buy it up to 5 fairly early in a chronicle. Such ultra-specialization does have its drawbacks, but obviously it has a lot of attraction for some players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a Discipline at 5 on character creation <b>is</b> possible, though you'll have nothing else basically - all 3 starting dots in the one of your preference, 14 freebies to rise it from 3 to 5, player would even have 1 freebie left for an extra background or Humanity dot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> Not every ST might be ok with that kind of min-maxing (even with no flaws involved), but i remember it being quite doable from a mechanical perspective in pretty much all editions.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-09-2023, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T13:13:17-07:00","id":1523093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523061#post1523061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a Discipline at 5 on character creation <b>is</b> possible, though you'll have nothing else basically - all 3 starting dots in the one of your preference, 14 freebies to rise it from 3 to 5, player would even have 1 freebie left for an extra background or Humanity dot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> Not every ST might be ok with that kind of min-maxing (even with no flaws involved), but i remember it being quite doable from a mechanical perspective in pretty much all editions.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically enough it can be somewhat XP efficient to max out a discipline from character generation, depending on playstyle and build.<br /> <br /> If you put one dot in each discipline and burn XP to max each, it would cost 150 XP post character generation. On the other hand, if you were to burn your freebies and max a single discipline, the cost is only 120 XP which is not an insignificant savings. Though as stated before the lack of 4th and 5th dots in certain abilities has to be build friendly.<br /> <br /> I made this approach work with a Tremere Seer build who had five ranks in Auspex from character generation. The Chantry where the character's haven was located is heavily warded and I spent the Background dots on an Ally/Retainer to get a loyalist Gargoyle bodyguard. It was an interesting character to play since everything had to be approached in an asymmetrical manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T18:56:12-07:00","id":1523113,"title":"","content":"I definitely think it's possible for an Ancillae to have maxed out a Discipline. Especially on the upper end of things, like 200+ years of age. Very feasible.<br /> <br /> What I'd probably say is that the character would probably be well known among local Kindred as having been very active in their younger nights, if they aren't active now. The kind of Kindred who went on a lot of adventures to establish themselves, and in the process became very powerful very quickly. As others have stated, most Ancillae and Elders avoid taking risks. They find their niche in Kindred society, then spend years slowly accumulating influence.<br /> <br /> The kind of Ancillae that topped off a Discipline is one who led an interesting unlife. Their place in Kindred society, and their relationships with other Kindred, should reflect that. They should have history, and maybe more than a few enemies (or at least rivals).<br /> <br /> It also matters a great deal <i>which</i> Discipline the Ancillae has maxed out.<br /> <br /> Something like the physical Disciplines would make them a martial threat (or, in the case of Fortitude, very tanky), but not greatly stand-out aside from this. It might imply they're a veteran of some major local conflict, like a Sabbat crusade, a violent Camarilla power struggle, or prolonged conflict with Lupines.<br /> <br /> High Dominate implies the character is a <i>bastard</i>. You don't typically need higher than Dominate 3 for most Kindred matters. There's little morally defensible reason, if any, to be able to hollow out a person's will or hijack their body. A Dominate 5 Ancillae is likely a controlling, domineering personality, with few scruples.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 5 means they're not just able to come and go where they please, but able to plausibly remain hidden even against Kindred with Auspex 5. So unless they're an Elder with Elder levels of Auspex, most Kindred will be very careful what they say or do. Because the Ancillae in question could be around, difficult or impossible to perceive. Alternatively, local Kindred are at best vaguely aware of the Ancillae, and almost never think of them. Because the character is almost always skulking about unseen. Beneath the notice of most Kindred, as they rarely make themselves known. Implying they are harmless, or <i>extremely</i> dangerous.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy 5, meanwhile, makes the Tremere in question very relevant, especially within the Pyramid. To achieve that level of blood magic mastery requires not merely loads of time and experience, but access to higher orders of occult knowledge. Implying they're either well connected/regarded within Clan Tremere, or they've acquired knowledge in some other fashion that makes them highly valuable. Valuable and suspicious. It's possible, especially in relatively new Clan holdings, that they're already the leader of a Chantry, or are being considered for same. This is a double-edged sword, as rival blood magicians (in and out of Clan &amp; House Tremere) seek to undermine or steal from them, or hold a grudge at having been passed over by some &quot;young&quot; upstart. Alternatively, they may have been sent to the local area, to head up a Chantry, simply to get them out of the way. Let the obvious arcane prodigy carve out a new center of Tremere power, rather than disrupt existing Clan power structures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T21:12:08-07:00","id":1523117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523113#post1523113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also matters a great deal <i>which</i> Discipline the Ancillae has maxed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though some disciplines it might be easier to downplay or outright hide one's actual degree of mastery than others, might be said. Obfuscate for sure, Dominate depending on how careful one is - as an aside, if one is not, it might backfire fast as your mere continued existence turns into a source of paranoia for everyone else (but that's partly because i tend to go utterly deep layer Jyhad level of evil if a character ever gets Dominate 4+).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523113#post1523113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgy 5, meanwhile, makes the Tremere in question very relevant, especially within the Pyramid. To achieve that level of blood magic mastery requires not merely loads of time and experience, but access to higher orders of occult knowledge. Implying they're either well connected/regarded within Clan Tremere, or they've acquired knowledge in some other fashion that makes them highly valuable. Valuable and suspicious. It's possible, especially in relatively new Clan holdings, that they're already the leader of a Chantry, or are being considered for same. This is a double-edged sword, as rival blood magicians (in and out of Clan &amp; House Tremere) seek to undermine or steal from them, or hold a grudge at having been passed over by some &quot;young&quot; upstart. Alternatively, they may have been sent to the local area, to head up a Chantry, simply to get them out of the way. Let the obvious arcane prodigy carve out a new center of Tremere power, rather than disrupt existing Clan power structures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly good points. What reminds me - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Peter_Dorfman\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a>, while in the 300s nowadays, was still in the late 200s when his stats came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T22:02:46-07:00","id":1523119,"title":"","content":"I tend to work on this disciplines template<br /> <br /> Neonate 4-6<br /> <br /> Anchilli 6-12<br /> <br /> Elder 12-20<br /> <br /> i also tend to have less out of clan disciplines than standard vtm npcs presented in the books. With this in mind its fairly common for an anchilli to have a 5 dot in clan power.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T23:00:50-07:00","id":1523122,"title":"","content":"I had even at the start of the chronicle and it is common to see multiple 5s in Neonates let alone Ancillas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T09:31:05-07:00","id":1523137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523122#post1523122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had even at the start of the chronicle and it is common to see multiple 5s in Neonates let alone Ancillas.</div> </div> </div> </div>How were you able to justify a player character having multiple 5 stats to start with? In one or two areas I could see such as being very athletic, charming, intelligent or having a natural talent for a particular discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T09:39:31-07:00","id":1523139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523119#post1523119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to work on this disciplines template<br /> <br /> Neonate 4-6<br /> <br /> Anchilli 6-12<br /> <br /> Elder 12-20<br /> <br /> i also tend to have less out of clan disciplines than standard vtm npcs presented in the books. With this in mind its fairly common for an anchilli to have a 5 dot in clan power.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I'm aiming for with my Malkavian that he is going to max out his Obfuscate Discipline very soon with Presence later down the road as he has a natural talent with that Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T04:17:21-07:00","id":1523168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523041-is-it-plausible-that-an-older-ancilla-could-have-5-dots-in-one-discipline?p=1523137#post1523137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How were you able to justify a player character having multiple 5 stats to start with? In one or two areas I could see such as being very athletic, charming, intelligent or having a natural talent for a particular discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, the one I used last time was a Ventrue Antitribu that was born for success and handpicked by Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, he got picked by Sabbat Antitribu Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T08:36:23-07:00","id":1523275,"title":"","content":"The number of dots for Cainites has always seemed to me like something difficult to put down as it would depend so much on the individual Cainite.<br /> <br /> But I would figure that the longer a Cainite has been, well, a Cainite then the less drive they have to do things and at 1000 years or above they have a serious problem with lethargy that is only broken by episodic flares of activity when something manages to stir them to action, before they sink back into lethargy again. That's been my favorite way to explain as to why ultra-old Cainites with godlike powers are not just being, well, godlike masters over everything and nothing can be done about it by any PC. And why the actions of neonates can have some impact rather than everything being run by elders who controls and foresees everything.<br /> <br /> But to ge to the question, I don't at all find it strange that an Ancillae would have at least one of the in-Clan Disciplines at 5 dots and the other two pretty high unless that Cainite is really operating on a basis where they don't have much use for their in-Clan Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T01:20:01-07:00","id":1523300,"title":"","content":"I'm quite surprised at the suggested power levels in this thread but I think it might be a playstyle thing.<br /> <br /> With campaigns I've played it's almost always been 3 dots at most for starting player characters. The only time I've played with a starting character with 5 dots in a discipline was a bit of a disaster as they overwhelmed all the other players.<br /> <br /> That said a two hundred year old Ancilla seems very likely to have one clan discipline at 5 unless they're the sort to spread them selves thinly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T02:38:54-07:00","id":1524799,"title":"","content":"When I was generating a bunch of NPCs for an adventure I created for V20, I needed a template to build from.<br /> <br /> Elders had a discipline spread of 6 / 5 / 4 / 3, with their lvl 6 power being inclan and one outclan.<br /> Ancillae had spread of 5 / 4 / 3 / 2, with one outclan.<br /> Strong neonates had 4 / 3 / 2 / 1, with one outclan.<br /> Normal neonates had 3 / 2 / 1.<br /> <br /> Worked well for me as a template to build lots of NPCs from. After the template, I of course adjusted things so the NPCs could have and do the things I needed them to have and do for the story to be compelling. But it was a good framework, hope it helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T15:10:40-08:00","id":1525222,"title":"","content":"It certainly does Pang4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T16:51:03-08:00","id":1525334,"title":"","content":"I think you can create a fairly realistic sheet just by imagining what a vampire needs to learn to survive. Your average Gangrel, for example, probably makes a mad dash to Earthmeld, frantically practicing Protean to achieve it, because until then they are doing things like sleeping in car trunks with tarps over them. Their existence is incredibly precarious until they can sleep wherever. After that, though, many might slow down, being able to actually enjoy nature, and almost lazily picking up dots in Survival, Awareness, and Stealth.<br /> <br /> Your average Ventrue is going to neglect disciplines and focus on whatever mundane skills he was embraced for such as business, as well as learning etiquette as quickly as possible. It is likely pretty common for some modern American Psycho type to begin with zero etiquette, and then race to etiquette 5 as quickly as they can, simply to avoid being killed by annoyed older Ventrue. After that many would focus on Fortitude, not for the physical durability, but for the ability to increasingly resist mind-manipulation, something invaluable in a clan of suffocating manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T13:38:07-08:00","id":1525359,"title":"","content":"wile five dots in most disciplines is impressive, most Ancilla will get more out of having a bunch more disciplines at rank 3, above rank 3 and the powers tend to be more useful for playing Eldar power games, there are exceptions, like Protean, Obfuscate and Thaumaturgy or the signature disciplines of the independent Clans and Bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28255-dropbear","name":"DropBear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T08:50:05-08:00","id":1525512,"title":"","content":"It depends on how you handle experience, both PC and NPC. <br /> <br /> On some Revised book (I think it was the Storyteller book) it suggests that an NPC should have a grand total of points in Disciplines equal to the square root of his age. Thus, an Ancilla should have about 14 points in Disciplines, so it's perfectly fine that he's spent 5 points in one Discipline. Also, as someone has mentioned before, is likely that he or she's going to be known as a powerful player, unless he goes the Lodin way and hides his true level of power (which can be smart).<br /> <br /> For a long time, in V20 I've run experience the following way as the standard experience system gets too much power too fast for the PCs. These days when I run V20 I just assign 1 XP per session flat when actively playing, and 1 XP/year in downtime. So, when I want to design an NPC I will generate it as a regular neonate PC and add its age in XP. 200 XP may be more than enough to get a Discipline to 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26110-ramon-nogueras","name":"Ramon Nogueras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T09:44:28-08:00","id":1525517,"title":"","content":"I did that in Aberrant way back when with my first character who carefully hid how much more powerful he really was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T13:50:14-08:00","id":1525655,"title":"","content":"Given how my players always want to max-out their disciplines, Ancilla? no, Neonates have a five-dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}